    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **James Wood** stands as our premier offensive anchor with a massive 74.79 score. His matchup against Alcantara presents the perfect storm: a 4.41 xERA pitcher coupled with a slow delivery that essentially gift-wraps stolen base opportunities for our elite speed asset. Sitting atop the lineup, **James Wood** is in a prime position to capitalize on run-scoring potential. **Corbin Carroll** also clears the 60-point threshold, thriving despite a tougher matchup against Sheehan. The combination of a favorable park adjustment and his high-end xwOBA makes **Corbin Carroll** a must-start, as his ability to manufacture SBs remains the cornerstone of our strategy in this 5x5 format.\n\nWe are navigating a narrow margin in the UTIL spot, where **Vinnie Pasquantino** (56.70) holds the floor against Richardson. While the opposing xERA of 2.83 is daunting, the +14% dynamic platoon boost for **Vinnie Pasquantino** keeps him ahead of our bench options. The closest exclusion was **Kyle Karros**, who landed at 38.93; while he shows promise, his status in the #9 hole and an unfavorable matchup against Soriano pushed him just below our 40-point \"Zebras\" floor. We are opting to bench **Kyle Karros**, **Cole Young**, and **Zach McKinstry** to preserve our game caps, as their lack of lineup density renders them inefficient starts for today's specific conditions.\n\nRisk mitigation remains the theme for the rest of our lineup. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Brice Turang** are hovering near our marginal threshold, with both suffering from the negative impact of facing Sheehan and Roupp, respectively. While **Brice Turang** is hampered by an elite opposing catcher\u2014reducing his SB efficiency projection\u2014his #3 spot in the order preserves his value. **Josh Naylor** provides a stable mid-range play at 55.23, benefiting from a +6% order boost, but we are monitoring the weather closely as any wind shifts could further suppress his raw projection. With **Tyler Soderstrom** off the board today, our priority remains maximizing the high-ceiling output of **James Wood** and **Corbin Carroll** while keeping our utility slots optimized for platoon advantages.",
